29,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"It seems that when there's no clear person to blame for bike damage, complaints just fade away. However, charging fees can create real social divides.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Oh dear, it's quite a mess. People are shifting each other's bikes every morning, and some poor souls are leaving their saddles in the rain.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,May,,"The building account is practically empty for capital work. Also, the ward park is expensive and has a huge waiting list.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,George,,"The paperwork for current collections is already a chore. Plus, those fancy double-tier racks require physical effort and regular maintenance.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Mio,,I found out that the same people have had the best spots for five years! But the daily riders say they'd actually prefer to pay for a spot.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, if the building account is empty, any new equipment would require a levy. That might be a point of contention for some residents.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, it's so sad that some people feel left out. We really need a way to make the morning routine more peaceful for everyone.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, if the treasurer is already struggling, we shouldn't add more complex billing. But we can't ignore that people are willing to pay.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,George,,"@Shizue, if we introduce a system that requires constant policing or heavy lifting, it will just fail like the last ones did.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shizue, the rain thing sounds awful! We should definitely try to make it fairer so the same people aren't always getting wet bikes.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@George, I agree. A system that creates administrative burnout or social resentment is a failure. We need something low-maintenance.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, that is very true. A gentle approach is always best to keep the harmony in our lovely building.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,May,,"@Mio, it's interesting that the daily riders are open to paying. Maybe there's a way to use that to our advantage?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,George,,"@May, as long as it doesn't turn into a full-time job for the association. Simplicity is the only way to ensure sustainability.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@May, yes! If people want to pay, maybe we can use that money to fix the rain problem or get better racks!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
