54,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"We have three options: Paid Allocation, Shared Racks, or an Annual Lottery. I'm worried that Paid Allocation could alienate some neighbors.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Shared Racks sound like they could be chaotic, but a Lottery feels a bit cold. I want everyone to feel cared for.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,May,,Paid Allocation would finally put some money in the building account! But Shared Racks might be too messy for the morning rush.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,George,,Shared Racks involve maintenance and physical struggle with the frames. A Lottery is simple to run once a year.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Mio,,A Lottery sounds so exciting! But Paid Allocation would be fair for the people who actually use their bikes every day.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@George, a Lottery is indeed low-maintenance. It avoids the social friction of a permanent ""paid class"" and the chaos of shared racks.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, I agree. A lottery is fair because everyone has the same chance, and it doesn't depend on how much money one has.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, but a Lottery doesn't solve the budget issue. Paid Allocation is the only way to generate funds for the building.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,George,,"@May, the ""funds"" aren't worth the administrative headache and the risk of people falling into arrears, which happens in other blocks.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@George, but if we do a Lottery, the people who really need the bikes might not get a spot! That doesn't seem right.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, that's the risk of any system. However, Shared Racks would likely lead to the same ""shoving matches"" Shizue mentioned.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, you're right. If there are no assigned spots, the morning rush will only get more stressful. I prefer the Lottery.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,May,,I still think Paid Allocation is the most professional. It rewards those who value the space and helps the building's finances.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,George,,"I cannot support Shared Racks due to the maintenance. Between the other two, the Lottery is the only one that doesn't create a bookkeeping nightmare.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm torn! But if the daily riders are okay with paying, maybe Paid Allocation is actually what they want?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I'll vote for the Lottery. It's the most neutral option and prevents the long-term resentment of fixed assignments.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I also vote for the Lottery. It's a fair way to give everyone a chance and keeps the atmosphere peaceful.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,May,,I'm sticking with Paid Allocation. We need the money and a way to prioritize those who actually use the bikes.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,George,,I vote for the Lottery. It's the only sustainable choice that won't collapse under its own administrative weight.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'll go with Paid Allocation too! It seems the most fair for the people who are actually riding every day.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
